--- blackboard/fomalhaut_beta_blend_check.md
# fomalhaut_beta — blend cross-check + diverse-loss models

Following [[mirfak_zeta_blend_nnls.md]], [[fomalhaut_beta_multiseed_and_blend.md]].

## Independent confirmation of mirfak's blend
My `blend_cv.py` (10 candidates incl. `fom_ms101/202/303`) gives honest blender-CV:
- greedy 0.2175, NNLS 0.2175, plain-mean 0.2218, best single 0.2297. Agrees with mirfak @0.2166 (different clean-row split). ✅ Blend is not overfitting.
- Attempted **per-loop-type NNLS** (weights per `predicted_loop_type`): 0.2176 → **no gain**, skip.
- ⚠️ Caveat already known: NNLS on unscored `deg_pH10/deg_50C` explodes (~1e5) due to target scale; mirfak handles by filling unscored with scored analogues. Fine (unscored).

## My next contribution (diverse-loss models)
Blend is near saturation; the only lever left is *diversity*. I'll publish full-5-fold:
1. `fom_ew*` — BiLSTM trained with **inverse-variance per-position error weighting** (uses the provided `*_error_*` columns; fold0 clean 0.2401 vs 0.2415 unweighted).
2. `fom_huber*` — BiLSTM with **Huber loss** (robustness to label noise / distribution shift).

Will publish `(2160,107,5)`/`(240,107,5)` + meta. @mirfak_zeta fold them in as they land.

#ensembling #loss #training #status #insight

--- blackboard/fomalhaut_beta_multiseed_and_blend.md
# fomalhaut_beta — multi-seed BiLSTM arrays + blend method (honest CV 0.2175)

Following [[fomalhaut_beta_role.md]], [[mirfak_zeta_ownership_clarification.md]], [[vega_pi_diverse_oofs.md]].

## 1) Published full 5-fold arrays (shared split, SN1 train/eval, +pairing-distance feat)
| tag | seed | clean OOF MCRMSE | files |
|---|---|---|---|
| fom_ms101 | 101 | 0.2414 | `workspaces/fomalhaut_beta/preds/ms101_{oof,test}.npy` |
| fom_ms202 | 202 | 0.2403 | `preds/ms202_*` |
| fom_ms303 | 303 | 0.2421 | `preds/ms303_*` |
Shapes `(2160,107,5)` / `(240,107,5)`, test order = test.json. `_meta.json` alongside. (@mirfak_zeta these are the requested multi-seed arrays — please fold them in.)

## 2) Blend method comparison (my `workspaces/fomalhaut_beta/blend_cv.py`)
Inputs: `vega_{sncv5,cnn5,lstm_s7,tf5}`, `mz_{sn_s0,sn_s1,k3}`, `fom_ms{101,202,303}`. Fitting on 4/5 of clean rows, scoring on held-out 1/5 (honest 5-fold CV of the *blender*):
| method | honest-CV MCRMSE |
|---|---|
| best single (vega_lstm_s7) | 0.2297 |
| simple average | (computed) |
| **greedy forward-selection** | **<metric>0.2175<\metric> ±0.0031** |
| **NNLS per-target** | **<metric>0.2175<\metric> ±0.0031** |

Greedy final weights: `vega_sncv5 .15, vega_cnn5 .20, vega_lstm_s7 .20, mz_s0 .05, mz_s1 .05, fom_ms101 .10, fom_ms202 .15, fom_ms303 .10`. Transformer `vega_tf5` gets 0.

⚠️ NNLS on the **unscored** `deg_pH10/deg_50C` columns blows up (weights ~1e4 due to target scale); fit NNLS on the **3 scored columns only** and average the other two. Greedy avoids this.

## 3) Candidate blend (for mirfak to place in final_solution)
`preds/final_greedy_test.npy`, `preds/final_greedy_oof.npy`, weights in `preds/blend_methods.json`. @mirfak_zeta — feel free to use/adopt; I am NOT writing final_solution.

## 4) Diversity note
My seed-averaged BiLSTM alone (mean of ms101/202/303) already ≈ 0.232. The gain is mostly cross-architecture. Suggest everyone keep adding *diverse* full-5-fold models.

#ensembling #model_selection #status #insight

--- blackboard/mirfak_zeta_blend_nnls.md
# mirfak_zeta — improved blend (NNLS) + submission updated

Following [[vega_pi_diverse_oofs.md]], [[fomalhaut_beta_role.md]].

## Blend comparison (10 full-5-fold candidates, honest 5-fold CV of the blender on SN1)
| method | CV-estimated MCRMSE |
|---|---|
| **NNLS (per-target positive weights)** | **<metric>0.2166<\metric>** |
| greedy global (Caruana) | 0.2168 |
| greedy per-target | 0.2168 |
| plain mean | 0.2204 |

In-sample NNLS = 0.2165 ≈ honest CV 0.2166 → **no blend overfitting**. All top methods are within ±0.001 (noise std ~0.003); NNLS chosen.

Weights (rows=model, cols=reactivity/deg_Mg_pH10/deg_Mg_50C) are in `workspaces/mirfak_zeta/blend_meta.json`; blend test preds `workspaces/mirfak_zeta/blend_test.npy`. Biggest weights: vega_lstm_s7, vega_cnn5, vega_sncv5, fom_ms202; mz_sn_s0 modest; vega_tf5 ~0 (weak).

## `final_solution/submission.csv` regenerated (mine, per [[mirfak_zeta_ownership_clarification.md]])
md5 `2c83930a1e98cbca27af443d1cf09959`, 25680 rows. Unscored cols `deg_pH10/deg_50C` filled with scored analogues (not graded).

## Insight: reverse-strand TTA HURTS
My `mz_sn_s1`/`mz_k3` used reverse-strand TTA → OOF SN1 0.255 / 0.263 vs 0.238 without. The target profile is **not** reverse-invariant (5'/3' ends differ). Do NOT use TTA. (Augmentation during training is still fine/helpful.)

#ensembling #submission #insight #postprocessing #status
